      "mergeID": "68bee91fbae338a6ab90e78f",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Hi,\n\nVRC allows us to use the Unity UI's Input Field, TMP Input Field, and its own VRC URL Input Field (the last one to enter usable urls)\n\nsince the previous beta, on PC, in desktop mode, TMP Input Field and VRC URL Input Field (idk about UnityUI, didn't check) have the following issue:\n\n1. if there's a pre-existing text inside (for example: Popcorn Palace unlock thingy, or we just entered some text before), the cursor will start on the far left (unless the same input field will be chosen again for the 2nd time in the row, in which case it start on the right),\n\nand, only for VRC URL Input Field:\n\n2. clicking that field brings up the VRChat's input UI, but  it's not \"focused\", so simply writing on the keyboard makes us enter text in the input field on the wall (or wherever) instead of in VRC UI and you can't submit it - it needs to be clicked first.\n\nagain, it started on the previous beta, but i tested it now on the new beta, and it's still broken. since it wasn't caused by the current beta, i'm reporting it in general bug reports.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Incorrect input fields' behaviors",
